//? Title: Subgraph matching: actual injective assignments and pruning
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find an injective adjacency-preserving mapping from a pattern into a target.
This API performs non-induced undirected matching: extra target edges are
permitted. Actual candidate pruning and backtracking histories explain success
or failure.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Assign pattern vertices in increasing index order. For each target candidate
reject an already used vertex, insufficient degree, or a missing target edge
required by an already assigned pattern neighbor. Recurse on surviving
assignments and undo them after a failed child. Return the first complete
injection. Pattern nonedges impose no constraint, so a three-vertex path maps
into a triangle. Normalization symmetrizes listed directions, removes duplicate
edges and ignores loops. Worst-case injection search is exponential; this
implementation also stores quadratic dense adjacency matrices.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/subgraph_isomorphism_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/subgraph_isomorphism.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<std::vector<int>> p{{1}, {0, 2}, {1}}, t{{1, 2}, {0, 2}, {0, 1}};
    auto r = a::subgraph_isomorphism_trace(3, p, 3, t);
    std::print("| actual depth | target | action | complete current mapping |\n| ---: | ---: | --- | --- " "|\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | `{}` |\n", s.depth, s.target, s.action,
                   s.mapping);
    std::print("Path into triangle found {}; nonedges are unconstrained.\n",
               r.match.found);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Path pattern into triangle target");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual candidate trials",
                                     r.candidate_trials));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual injection {}", r.match.mapping));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/subgraph_isomorphism_tiny.svg");
}
```
