> API and interpretation

All row counts, neighbor IDs and dense geometry are validated before
impossible-size early return. An empty pattern succeeds; a larger-than-target
pattern fails after validation. Captured adjacency and mappings are actual
native producer state. The API is explicitly non-induced, ignores loops and uses
union-of-directions undirected normalization; it does not solve directed,
labelled or induced matching.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Ullmann, An Algorithm for Subgraph Isomorphism, Journal of the ACM23 (1976),31-42|https://doi.org/10.1145/321921.321925]

